# Cloudflare Pages edge redirects.
# Next.js's server-side redirect() (used for old blog slugs via the
# `redirect` field in app/blog/posts.ts) doesn't work with static export —
# it needs a live server to intercept the redirect signal. These rules
# handle those redirects properly at the CDN edge instead (real HTTP 301).
#
# Keep this in sync with any `redirect:` entries in app/blog/posts.ts.
/blog/inde-ude /blog/overgang-mellem-ude-og-inde 301

# Old blog posts removed as duplicates (never had a `redirect:` entry since
# the post object itself was deleted, not renamed) — still indexed/linked
# externally, so redirect instead of letting them 404.
/blog/hvordan-vurderer-man-om-en-byggegrund-er-god /blog/valg-af-byggegrund 301
/blog/orangeri-ved-huset /blog/orangeri 301

# Inspirationskatalog PDF removed along with the whole katalog feature —
# send anyone who still has the old download link to the inspiration gallery.
/katalog-inspiration.pdf /inspiration 301
